WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.002
Our thoughts are with the families

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.903
who've lost loved ones.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.239
And we're also thinking and praying

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.107
for the people

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:09.409
who were injured in this attack.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.612
Including our police officers.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.781
So for an update on their condition,

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.816
I first would like to welcome Dr.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.218
Jason Smith,

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.653
chief medical officer at U of L Health.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:21.354
Dr.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:21.955
Smith,

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:25.725
thank you, Mayor.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.826
So from you,

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.228
though, health and you, the hospital,

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.996
I want to send my prayers

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:32.098
and thoughts out to all the families

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.333
that were affected yesterday.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.601
Both those we treated and

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.936
and unfortunately, those we did not.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.972
An update from us.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.273
We still have four patients

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:43.410
in the hospital to remain in the ICU

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.711
Officer will still

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.012
officer will still remains

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.547
in critical condition.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.281
But we have been able

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.549
to upgrade our other patient

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.684
in the ICU to stable condition.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.386
The other two remain in the hospital

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.687
being treated for non-life

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.488
threatening injuries.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.158
I want to thank my team again,

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:59.292
the emergency department,

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.061
physicians and nurses, my trauma

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.128
team of you, of our health

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.431
and all those who supported us yesterday.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.766
I also want to send a

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.402
thank you to the American Red Cross.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.871
We used 170 units of blood yesterday

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.873
to treat these victims

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.643
which far outstrips our hospital capacity

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.511
and their ability to get us

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.547
that blood to save those lives

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.948
helped save those lives.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.249
So I want to thank them for that.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.951
I won't get into too many specifics

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:25.852
about the patients

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.420
we're currently caring for.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.822
We did operate on

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:29.823
three of them yesterday.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:33.159
The required emergency operations

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.995
My team were absolute professionals.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.597
We trained for this.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.233
It's difficult to

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.335
it's very difficult to be able to process

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.737
what's going on during that time.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.106
And so the training that we do

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.307
with our emergency department,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.341
nurses and physicians,

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.510
our surgical services, our trauma teams,

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.412
the blood bank

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.848
all of that makes a huge difference

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.683
and being able to save those lives

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.218
because we have to act quickly.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.155
But I'll be honest,

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.792
caring for three shooting victims

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.461
plus the other that came in

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:11.131
is not an unsafe, frequent day for us.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.299
And the events surrounding

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.068
this made this obviously

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.003
much more difficult.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.105
But to be honest with you,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.807
we barely had to adjust our

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.774
operating room schedule

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.743
to be able to do this.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.979
That's how frequent we are

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.480
having to deal with gun violence

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.781
in our community.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.752
I'll tell you personally, I'm weary.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.320
I've been in Louisville for 15 years,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.222
all of it at University Hospital.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.090
For 15 years,

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.458
I've cared for victims of violence

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:40.059
and gunshot wounds.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.294
And people say, I'm tired,

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:43.263
but I'll be answer. It's more than tired.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.531
I'm weary.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:46.199
There's only so many times

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.301
you can walk into a room

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.135
and tell someone

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.403
they're not coming home tomorrow.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.540
And it just breaks your heart

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.841
when you hear someone screaming

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.510
Mommy or daddy.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.913
It just becomes too hard day in and day

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.581
out to be able to do that.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.917
Now, my team is fantastic.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.552
They're absolute professionals

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.253
and they're wonderful.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:09.856
But sooner or later

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.492
it catches up to everybody.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:13.893
You just can't keep doing

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.328
what we're doing

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.396
because you just can't

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.798
keep seeing these lives lost.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.900
You can't keep seeing all the people

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.835
with these horrific injuries

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.304
coming through the door

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.772
without doing something

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.739
to try and help them.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.342
And I don't know what the answers are.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.109
I'm a doctor.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.579
I don't know what the answers are.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:35.248
But to everyone who helps make policy,

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.617
both at state, city, federal,

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.786
I would simply ask you to do something,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.888
because doing nothing,

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:42.822
which is what we've been

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.123
doing, is not working.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.093
We have to do something

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.862
because this is just getting out of hand

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.264
across our city

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.033
and across this great nation of ours.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.603
Sorry, but you don't know

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.571
Peter.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.073
Yeah.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.140
So

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.809
he's still in the ICU.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.244
He's still sedated.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.346
And I again, I apologize.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.313
I am not going to release

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.315
any other information

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.583
for the patients

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.252
that we're still taking care of.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.152
Still in critical

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.153
still to save yesterday.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.755
The next 24 hours are going to be

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.923
very intense.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.691
Is that still the same set today?

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.058
Yes.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.460
So he's still in critical condition

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.194
in ICU.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:21.961
He's being treated

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.030
by our neurosurgery team,

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.398
being treated by our trauma team

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:27.367
at our anesthesia teams.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.701
And is still undergoing

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.403
a lot of care at bedside.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:30.903
Good news.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.672
We had another patient released.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.507
I know we talked a lot about the hurt

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:35.675
to see these people

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:36.142
receive

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:36.743
trauma care,

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.711
but the person was able to leave

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.146
and walk out of the hospital.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:40.847
How does that feel

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.649
to see the good part of this today?

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:44.651
Yeah, so, I

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:46.352
mean, the answer is, is that, you know,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.787
today we had for

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.656
we may have a three

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:50.957
the the ones that are doing

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.125
well are doing well.

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.193
And I think, you know, the work

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:54.961
that we do

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.862
with the physicians

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.631
and the nurses at the hospital

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.333
is just it's unbelievable

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.134
sometimes that people

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.468
that we're able to save these days,

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:03.636
we have partners

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.604
like the Red Cross

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:05.672
that can get us, you know,

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.040
170 units of blood

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.941
in a eight hour period of time.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:09.709
It's just

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.711
the coordination of the city

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:12.945
of the health care system

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.881
and of the hospital is

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.082
is outstanding

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.350
to be able to say that those

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.351
patients are going home.

